{
  "id": "S2E21",
  "season": 2,
  "episode": 21,
  "showTitle": "The Hard Saying",
  "title": "Laetare",
  "dates": "Monday, March 8 – Sunday, March 14, 2010",
  "logline": "A paperback Catechism read from the first page, three days to the Forum, and an empty stage where somebody hears it first; on Thursday, Miss Broussard has the floor, and on Saturday, something small, and his.",
  "previously": [
    {
      "text": "In the back row of Oceanography, Skye: “You don’t lie,” … “So you owe me.” … “You’re going to sit somewhere and explain it until I understand it. Slowly.”"
    },
    {
      "text": "In her car, Skye: “I understand it,” … “I don’t accept it. Those are different departments.” … “But this isn’t done.” On her dash, a new paperback Catechism, with a receipt for a bookmark."
    },
    {
      "text": "On her landing, Lena: “I mind. I’m telling you I mind so I don’t have to act like I don’t.” — You: “She says it isn’t done.” — Lena: “All right.” … “Saturday stands.”",
      "if": "s2e20_tell==\"candor\""
    },
    {
      "text": "On her landing, Lena: “I mind. I’m telling you I mind so I don’t have to act like I don’t.” — You: “Some of what she said is hers. I’m not going to give it to you.” — Lena: “Good. Keep hers.”",
      "if": "s2e20_tell==\"sincerity\""
    },
    {
      "text": "On her landing, Lena: “I mind. I’m telling you I mind so I don’t have to act like I don’t.” — You: “Ask me anything.” — Lena: “Did you tell her the truth?”",
      "if": "s2e20_tell==\"restraint\""
    },
    {
      "text": "On her landing, Lena: “I mind. I’m telling you I mind so I don’t have to act like I don’t.”",
      "if": "s2e20_tell!=\"candor\" && s2e20_tell!=\"sincerity\" && s2e20_tell!=\"restraint\""
    },
    {
      "text": "In Hollis 302, Hale: “This year’s motion is *That one can be good without God*. I am proposing it.” … “And Miss Broussard has volunteered to lose to me in public.”"
    },
    {
      "text": "Lena: “The wolf has a *for*, and nobody had to mean it. I grant you the wolf. Then the wolf can be damaged. He can’t be *wronged*.” … “I’m using that Thursday week. With attribution, Professor Costigan.”",
      "if": "duel.anscombe.rigor>=2 && s2e20_d2==\"press\" || duel.anscombe.rigor>=2 && s2e20_d2==\"reframe\""
    },
    {
      "text": "Lena: “There’s a creditor in the room, and you found him, sitting right across the table. I grant you him.” … “I’m using that Thursday week. With attribution, Professor Costigan.”",
      "if": "duel.anscombe.rigor>=2 && s2e20_d2!=\"press\" && s2e20_d2!=\"reframe\""
    },
    {
      "text": "Lena: “He *gave* it to me,” … “He was supposed to be you, Professor, and he sat in that chair and gave me my case.”",
      "if": "duel.anscombe.rigor<=1 && duel.anscombe.heart>=2"
    },
    {
      "text": "Hale: “And what does Miss Broussard say to the good atheist in the third row,” … “who will be real, and will be listening?”",
      "if": "duel.anscombe.rigor<=1 && duel.anscombe.heart<=1"
    },
    {
      "text": "On Ocean Road, you: “Will you let me take you out again? Saturday. I’m planning it.” — Lena: “Where?” — You: “Mine.” — Lena: “Then yes.”",
      "if": "s2e20_again==\"sincerity\""
    },
    {
      "text": "On Ocean Road, you: “Miss Broussard, I’m told the second form is due.” — Lena: “Where?” — You: “Mine.” — Lena: “Then yes.”",
      "if": "s2e20_again==\"wit\""
    },
    {
      "text": "On Ocean Road, you: “Again. Saturday.” — Lena: “Where?” — You: “Mine.” — Lena: “Then yes.”",
      "if": "s2e20_again==\"candor\""
    },
    {
      "text": "On Ocean Road, Lena: “Where?” — You: “Mine.” — Lena: “Then yes.”",
      "if": "s2e20_again!=\"sincerity\" && s2e20_again!=\"wit\" && s2e20_again!=\"candor\""
    }
  ],
